1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,370
Why was the writer's aunt surprised?
作者的姑母为什么感到惊讶？

2
00:00:13,370 --> 00:00:16,620
Why was the writer's aunt surprised?
作者的姑母为什么感到惊讶？

3
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:20,870
It was Sunday.
那是个星期天。

4
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,270
I never get up early on Sundays.
星期天我是从来不早起的。

5
00:00:25,030 --> 00:00:28,540
I sometimes stay in bed until lunchtime.
有时我要一直躺到吃午饭的时候。

6
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:33,510
Last Sunday I got up very late.
上个星期天，我起得很晚。

7
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,770
I looked out of the window.
我望望窗外。

8
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,600
It was dark outside.
外面一片昏暗。

9
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:44,950
'What a day!' I thought.
“鬼天气！”我想。

10
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:48,790
'It's raining again.'
“又下雨了。”

11
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:51,300
Just then, the telephone rang.
正在这时，电话铃响了。

12
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:54,040
It was my aunt Lucy.
是我的姑母露西打来的。

13
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:59,190
'I've just arrived by train,' she said.
“我刚下火车，”她说。

14
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:01,230
'I'm coming to see you.'
“我这就来看你。”

15
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,470
'But I'm still having breakfast,' I said.
“但我还在吃早饭，”我说。

16
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,990
'What are you doing?' she asked.
“你在干什么？”她问道。

17
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:15,390
'I'm having breakfast,' I repeated.
“我正在吃早饭，”我又说了一遍。

18
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:19,170
'Dear me,' she said.
“天啊，”她说。

19
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:23,690
'Do you always get up so late? It's one o'clock!'
“你总是起得这么晚吗？现在已经一点钟了！”
